  evidencePrefab: {fileID: 6586202626002414144, guid: b02f6cf486235c440987b4f4073b828e, type: 3}
  storyName: N/A
  storyDate: N/A
  storyDescription: "I don\u2019t have a car so I always have to walk down this sketchy
    trail after work. I\u2019m not really worried about people around here though,
    for me it's the animals. My brother, who works for the national park around here,
    has been telling me that animals are being found all over the woods mangled.
    Not even eaten as if they were just killed and left there. It was wildlife at
    first but recently someone\u2019s dog ran into the woods and wasn\u2019t found
    until a few days later in the same fashion. Last night, as I was walking down
    the trail, I was unsettled by the silence in the air. I tried to keep my composure,
    but the rustling in the bushes caught my attention followed by an unnatural gargled
    growl, as if it struggled to let out noise. All I saw in the bushes were eyes
    glowing in the dark. Eyes of a predator. I booked it to my house only barely
    making it inside before there was a furious crash into the door. A frenzy of
    scraping at the door eventually gave way before I assumed the thing gave up."
